IMPORT prelude

-- Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 (Cth) -- the rules a discloser or witness meets.
--
-- Based on content from the Federal Register of Legislation: "Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013", Compilation No. 20
-- (compilation date 4 June 2026, register id C2026C00225), Commonwealth of Australia, licensed under CC BY 4.0
-- (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Quotations are from the deposited plain-text conversion at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/C2013A00133.txt.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.
--
-- Negatives follow the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 (docs/ENCODING-GUIDE.md section 5): JUST FALSE where the
-- text itself says no; NOTHING where it does not answer, each tagged "NOTHING-kind" with the reason. Every function
-- here but one answers a definition the Act closes ("means", "has the meaning given by"), an "if" or "only if"
-- condition, or a flat negative, so it returns a plain BOOLEAN whose FALSE is the text's own no (NOTES.md, Negatives).

§ `Public Interest Disclosure Act 2013 -- the discloser and the witness`

§§ `s 69 and s 70 -- public official`

-- s 69(1) "a public official means an individual mentioned in column 1 of an item of the following table". Items 1-20
-- (there are no items 5 and 6), grouped where the agency they belong to is the only difference. s 69(4): "Despite
-- subsections (1) and (2), the following are not public officials: (a) a judicial officer; (b) a member of a Royal
-- Commission; (c) a member of Parliament; (d) a person employed under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984."
DECLARE `What I am or was` IS ONE OF
    `an APS employee in a Department`
    `a member of staff of an agency other than a Department`
    `the Secretary of a Department`
    `the principal officer of an agency other than a Department`
    `an individual who constitutes or is a member of a prescribed authority other than a court`
    `a director of a Commonwealth company`
    `a member of the Defence Force or a cadet or officer or instructor in the Australian Defence Force Cadets`
    `an AFP appointee`
    `a Parliamentary Service employee`
    `employed by the Commonwealth otherwise than as an APS employee and performing duties for an agency`
    `a statutory officeholder`
    `a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract or its officer or employee providing services for the contract`
    `an individual exercising powers or performing functions conferred by a Commonwealth law outside the excluded Acts`
    `an individual exercising powers or performing functions under a law in force in Norfolk Island or Christmas Island or the Cocos Islands`
    `the Registrar or a Deputy Registrar of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Corporations`
    `a judicial officer`
    `a member of a Royal Commission`
    `a member of Parliament`
    `a person employed under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984`
    `none of these`

GIVEN w IS A `What I am or was`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69(4) -- excluded from being a public official` w IF
        w EQUALS `a judicial officer`
    OR  w EQUALS `a member of a Royal Commission`
    OR  w EQUALS `a member of Parliament`
    OR  w EQUALS `a person employed under the Members of Parliament (Staff) Act 1984`

-- A "means" definition with a flat exclusion: outside the table, or within s 69(4), the text says no.
GIVEN w IS A `What I am or was`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 69 -- a public official` w IF
        (NOT (`s 69(4) -- excluded from being a public official` w))
    AND (NOT (w EQUALS `none of these`))

-- s 70(1): an authorised officer may determine in writing "that this Act has effect, and is taken always to have had
-- effect, in relation to the disclosure of the information by the individual, as if the individual had been a public
-- official when the person obtained the information." s 70(3A): "This section does not apply if the individual is" one
-- of the four excluded persons. Whether to determine is the officer's call: asked as a fact (has it been made).
GIVEN w IS A `What I am or was`, `s 70 determination made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1)(a) -- the discloser is or has been a public official` w `s 70 determination made` IF
        `s 69 -- a public official` w
    OR  (    `s 70 determination made`
         AND (NOT (`s 69(4) -- excluded from being a public official` w)))

§§ `ss 29-33 -- disclosable conduct`

-- s 29(1) "Disclosable conduct is conduct of a kind mentioned in the following table that is conduct: (a) engaged in by
-- an agency; or (b) engaged in by a public official, in connection with his or her position as a public official; or
-- (c) engaged in by a contracted service provider for a Commonwealth contract, in connection with entering into, or
-- giving effect to, that contract." s 30(1): for a contractor's officer or employee, conduct is "in connection with his
-- or her position" only if it is in connection with entering into or giving effect to the contract.
DECLARE `Whose conduct` IS ONE OF
    `an agency`
    `a public official in connection with their position`
    `a public official not in connection with their position`
    `a contracted service provider in connection with entering into or giving effect to the Commonwealth contract`
    `someone else`

-- The table in s 29(1) (items 1-10) and s 29(2)(a), (b).
DECLARE `Kind of conduct` IS ONE OF
    `conduct that contravenes a law of the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory`
    `conduct in a foreign country that contravenes a law in force there that applies to them and corresponds to an ACT law`
    `conduct that perverts the course of justice or involves corruption`
    `maladministration such as conduct on improper motives or that is unreasonable or unjust or oppressive or negligent`
    `an abuse of public trust`
    `fabrication or falsification or plagiarism or deception in scientific research or misconduct in scientific analysis or evaluation or advice`
    `conduct that results in the wastage of relevant money or property or of the money or property of a prescribed authority`
    `conduct that unreasonably results in a danger or an increased risk of danger to the health or safety of a person`
    `conduct that results in a danger or an increased risk of danger to the environment`
    `conduct of a kind prescribed by the PID rules`
    `a public official abusing their position as a public official`
    `conduct of a public official that could if proved give reasonable grounds for disciplinary action ending their engagement or appointment`
    `none of these`

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(2) -- a kind added for public officials` k IF
        k EQUALS `a public official abusing their position as a public official`
    OR  k EQUALS `conduct of a public official that could if proved give reasonable grounds for disciplinary action ending their engagement or appointment`

-- s 29(1) and (2) before the exclusions. (1): a table kind, by one of the three actors. (2)(a), (b): "conduct engaged
-- in by a public official" -- (b) is not limited to conduct in connection with the position (finding 3).
GIVEN who IS A `Whose conduct`, k IS A `Kind of conduct`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(1) and (2) -- conduct of a disclosable kind` who k IF
        (    (NOT (k EQUALS `none of these`))
         AND (NOT (`s 29(2) -- a kind added for public officials` k))
         AND (    who EQUALS `an agency`
              OR  who EQUALS `a public official in connection with their position`
              OR  who EQUALS `a contracted service provider in connection with entering into or giving effect to the Commonwealth contract`))
    OR  (    `s 29(2) -- a kind added for public officials` k
         AND (    who EQUALS `a public official in connection with their position`
              OR  who EQUALS `a public official not in connection with their position`))

-- s 29A: personal work-related conduct is conduct by one public official in relation to another that occurs in relation
-- to the second official's engagement, appointment, employment or functions and "has, or would tend to have, personal
-- implications for the second official". s 29(2A): "Despite subsections (1) and (2), personal work-related conduct is not
-- disclosable conduct unless: (a) the conduct would constitute taking a reprisal ..., or an offence under section 19 ...;
-- or (b) the conduct: (i) is of such a significant nature that it would undermine public confidence in an agency (or
-- agencies); or (ii) has other significant implications for an agency (or agencies)." (b) is a judgment: an input.
GIVEN `personal work-related` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reprisal or s 19 offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `significant for an agency` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29(2A) -- excluded as personal work-related conduct` `personal work-related` `a reprisal or s 19 offence` `significant for an agency` IF
        `personal work-related`
    AND (NOT (`a reprisal or s 19 offence` OR `significant for an agency`))

-- Disclosable conduct: s 29 after s 29(2A) and the three exclusions. s 31: "conduct is not disclosable conduct if it
-- relates only to" a government policy, ministerial (or Speaker or President) action, or the spending on them, "with
-- which a person disagrees". s 32(1): "Despite section 29, conduct is not disclosable conduct if it is" conduct of a
-- judicial officer, judicial-power conduct of court staff, tribunal-power conduct of tribunal members and staff, or
-- other court or tribunal conduct unless administrative and not about managing or hearing matters. s 33: conduct of an
-- intelligence agency, or its officials, in the proper performance of its functions or exercise of its powers.
GIVEN who IS A `Whose conduct`, k IS A `Kind of conduct`,
      `personal work-related` IS A BOOLEAN, `a reprisal or s 19 offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `significant for an agency` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `only a disagreement with policy or ministerial action` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `excluded court or tribunal conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `proper intelligence agency conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 29 -- disclosable conduct` who k `personal work-related` `a reprisal or s 19 offence` `significant for an agency` `only a disagreement with policy or ministerial action` `excluded court or tribunal conduct` `proper intelligence agency conduct` IF
        `s 29(1) and (2) -- conduct of a disclosable kind` who k
    AND (NOT (`s 29(2A) -- excluded as personal work-related conduct` `personal work-related` `a reprisal or s 19 offence` `significant for an agency`))
    AND (NOT `only a disagreement with policy or ministerial action`)
    AND (NOT `excluded court or tribunal conduct`)
    AND (NOT `proper intelligence agency conduct`)

§§ `s 34 -- authorised internal recipient`

-- s 34 table column 1: what the conduct relates to (s 35: the agency, or an official belonging to it at the time,
-- engaged in it).
DECLARE `What the conduct relates to` IS ONE OF
    `an agency other than an intelligence agency or the Ombudsman or the IGIS`
    `an intelligence agency`
    `the Ombudsman`
    `the IGIS`

-- Who received the disclosure. The first five are authorised officers (s 36: the principal officer, or an official
-- appointed in writing by the principal officer).
DECLARE `Who I disclosed to` IS ONE OF
    `an authorised officer of the agency the conduct relates to`
    `an authorised officer of the agency I belong to or last belonged to`
    `an authorised officer of the Ombudsman`
    `an authorised officer of the IGIS`
    `an authorised officer of another investigative agency that has power to investigate the disclosure otherwise than under this Act`
    `my supervisor`
    `an Australian legal practitioner`
    `a foreign public official`
    `anyone else`

-- s 34 "The following table sets out who is an authorised internal recipient": a closed table, so outside it the text
-- says no. Item 1 (a)-(d); (c) "except if paragraph (ca) applies"; item 2 (a)-(c), which does not include the
-- discloser's own agency (finding 4); items 3 and 4.
GIVEN about IS A `What the conduct relates to`, r IS A `Who I disclosed to`,
      `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I believe it is about intelligence functions of AUSTRAC or Home Affairs or the AFP` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I believe the IGIS should investigate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `some information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 34 -- an authorised internal recipient` about r `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate` `I believe it is about intelligence functions of AUSTRAC or Home Affairs or the AFP` `I believe the IGIS should investigate` `some information is intelligence information` MEANS
    CONSIDER about
    WHEN `an agency other than an intelligence agency or the Ombudsman or the IGIS` THEN
             r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the agency the conduct relates to`
         OR  r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the agency I belong to or last belonged to`
         OR  (    r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the Ombudsman`
              AND `I believe the Ombudsman should investigate`
              AND (NOT `item 1(ca) applies`))
         OR  (    r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the IGIS`
              AND `item 1(ca) applies`)
         OR  r EQUALS `an authorised officer of another investigative agency that has power to investigate the disclosure otherwise than under this Act`
    WHEN `an intelligence agency` THEN
             r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the agency the conduct relates to`
         OR  (    r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the IGIS`
              AND `I believe the IGIS should investigate`)
         OR  (    r EQUALS `an authorised officer of another investigative agency that has power to investigate the disclosure otherwise than under this Act`
              AND (NOT `some information is intelligence information`))
    WHEN `the Ombudsman` THEN
             r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the agency the conduct relates to`
         OR  r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the Ombudsman`
    WHEN `the IGIS` THEN
             r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the agency the conduct relates to`
         OR  r EQUALS `an authorised officer of the IGIS`
    WHERE
        `item 1(ca) applies` MEANS
                `I believe it is about intelligence functions of AUSTRAC or Home Affairs or the AFP`
            AND `I believe the IGIS should investigate`

§§ `s 26 -- public interest disclosure`

-- s 26(1): "A disclosure of information is a public interest disclosure if: (a) the disclosure is made by a person (the
-- discloser) who is, or has been, a public official; and (b) the recipient ... is a person of the kind referred to in
-- column 2 of an item of the following table; and (c) all the further requirements set out in column 3 of that item are
-- met." With s 8 ("public interest disclosure has the meaning given by Subdivision A"), the items and s 26(1A) are the
-- whole definition: outside them the text says no.

-- Item 1, internal disclosure. Recipient: "An authorised internal recipient, or a supervisor of the discloser". (a) "The
-- information tends to show, or the discloser believes on reasonable grounds that the information tends to show, one or
-- more instances of disclosable conduct." (b) "The disclosure is not made in the course of performing the discloser's
-- ordinary functions as a public official."
GIVEN `a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `to an authorised internal recipient` IS A BOOLEAN, `to my supervisor` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the course of my ordinary functions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1) item 1 -- an internal disclosure` `a public official` `to an authorised internal recipient` `to my supervisor` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `in the course of my ordinary functions` IF
        `a public official`
    AND (`to an authorised internal recipient` OR `to my supervisor`)
    AND `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
    AND (NOT `in the course of my ordinary functions`)

-- Item 2, external disclosure. Recipient: "Any person other than a foreign public official". (a) as item 1; (b) an
-- earlier internal disclosure of information that "consisted of, or included, the information now disclosed"; (c) one of
-- (i) a Division 2 investigation the discloser believes on reasonable grounds was inadequate, (ii) an investigation
-- whose response the discloser believes on reasonable grounds was inadequate -- but by s 26(2A) a response is "taken ...
-- not to be inadequate to the extent that the response involves action that has been, is being, or is to be taken by" a
-- Minister, the Speaker or the President -- or (iii) a required Division 2 investigation not completed within the s 52
-- time limit; (e) "not, on balance, contrary to the public interest" (a judgment, made with regard to s 26(3)); (f) "No
-- more information is publicly disclosed than is reasonably necessary to identify one or more instances of disclosable
-- conduct"; (h) no intelligence information; (i) "None of the conduct ... relates to an intelligence agency, except ACIC".
GIVEN `a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `to a foreign public official` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `I disclosed it internally before` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Division 2 investigation was inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the response to the investigation was inadequate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the inadequacy is only action by a Minister or the Speaker or the President` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the investigation was not completed within the time limit` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `not on balance contrary to the public interest` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no more than reasonably necessary` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `some information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency other than ACIC` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1) item 2 -- an external disclosure` `a public official` `to a foreign public official` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `I disclosed it internally before` `the Division 2 investigation was inadequate` `the response to the investigation was inadequate` `the inadequacy is only action by a Minister or the Speaker or the President` `the investigation was not completed within the time limit` `not on balance contrary to the public interest` `no more than reasonably necessary` `some information is intelligence information` `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency other than ACIC` IF
        `a public official`
    AND (NOT `to a foreign public official`)
    AND `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
    AND `I disclosed it internally before`
    AND (    `the Division 2 investigation was inadequate`
         OR  (    `the response to the investigation was inadequate`
              AND (NOT `the inadequacy is only action by a Minister or the Speaker or the President`))
         OR  `the investigation was not completed within the time limit`)
    AND `not on balance contrary to the public interest`
    AND `no more than reasonably necessary`
    AND (NOT `some information is intelligence information`)
    AND (NOT `some conduct relates to an intelligence agency other than ACIC`)

-- Item 3, emergency disclosure. Recipient: "Any person other than a foreign public official". (a) the discloser "believes
-- on reasonable grounds that the information concerns a substantial and imminent danger to the health or safety of one or
-- more persons or to the environment"; (b) "The extent of the information disclosed is no greater than is necessary to
-- alert the recipient"; (c) with no earlier internal disclosure, "exceptional circumstances justifying the discloser's
-- failure to make such an internal disclosure"; (d) with one, "exceptional circumstances justifying this disclosure being
-- made before a disclosure investigation of the internal disclosure is completed"; (f) no intelligence information.
-- (d) once the investigation is complete has nothing to justify: taken as met (fork F3). No requirement that the
-- information concern disclosable conduct (finding 1).
GIVEN `a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `to a foreign public official` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `no more than necessary to alert the recipient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I disclosed it internally before` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the investigation of my internal disclosure is complete` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `exceptional circumstances justify it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `some information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1) item 3 -- an emergency disclosure` `a public official` `to a foreign public official` `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger` `no more than necessary to alert the recipient` `I disclosed it internally before` `the investigation of my internal disclosure is complete` `exceptional circumstances justify it` `some information is intelligence information` IF
        `a public official`
    AND (NOT `to a foreign public official`)
    AND `I believe there is a substantial and imminent danger`
    AND `no more than necessary to alert the recipient`
    AND (    `exceptional circumstances justify it`
         OR  (`I disclosed it internally before` AND `the investigation of my internal disclosure is complete`))
    AND (NOT `some information is intelligence information`)

-- Item 4, legal practitioner disclosure. Recipient: "An Australian legal practitioner". (a) "made for the purpose of
-- obtaining legal advice, or professional assistance, from the recipient in relation to the discloser having made, or
-- proposing to make, a public interest disclosure"; (b) "If the discloser knew, or ought reasonably to have known, that
-- any of the information has a national security or other protective security classification, the recipient holds the
-- appropriate level of security clearance"; (c) no intelligence information.
GIVEN `a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `to an Australian legal practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `for advice about a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I knew or ought to have known some information is classified` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the practitioner holds the clearance` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `some information is intelligence information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1) item 4 -- a legal practitioner disclosure` `a public official` `to an Australian legal practitioner` `for advice about a public interest disclosure` `I knew or ought to have known some information is classified` `the practitioner holds the clearance` `some information is intelligence information` IF
        `a public official`
    AND `to an Australian legal practitioner`
    AND `for advice about a public interest disclosure`
    AND (    (NOT `I knew or ought to have known some information is classified`)
         OR  `the practitioner holds the clearance`)
    AND (NOT `some information is intelligence information`)

-- s 26(1A): "also a public interest disclosure if: (a) the disclosure is made by a person who is, or has been, a public
-- official; and (b) the information tends to show, or the discloser believes on reasonable grounds that the information
-- tends to show, one or more instances of disclosable conduct; and (c) the disclosure is a NACC disclosure." "NACC
-- disclosure" is borrowed from the National Anti-Corruption Commission Act 2022: a fact.
GIVEN `a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `it tends to show disclosable conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `a NACC disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26(1A) -- a NACC disclosure that is a public interest disclosure` `a public official` `it tends to show disclosable conduct` `a NACC disclosure` IF
        `a public official`
    AND `it tends to show disclosable conduct`
    AND `a NACC disclosure`

§§ `s 28 -- how a disclosure may be made`

-- s 28(1)-(3): "may be made orally or in writing", "anonymously", and "without the discloser asserting that the disclosure
-- is made for the purposes of this Act". (4): "This section does not apply to a public interest disclosure that is also a
-- NACC disclosure"; the note sends the reader to the NACC Act.
GIVEN `also a NACC disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 28 -- the form does not matter` `also a NACC disclosure` MEANS
    IF `also a NACC disclosure`
    -- NOTHING-kind: s 28(4) disapplies the section and points outside the sources (the NACC Act).
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 10-12 -- immunity of the discloser`

-- What the person might be made answerable for. The first four are what s 10(1) and (2) protect against; the rest are
-- what ss 11, 11A and 12 take outside s 10.
DECLARE `Liability faced` IS ONE OF
    `civil or criminal or administrative liability including disciplinary action for making it`
    `a contractual or other remedy or right enforced against me on the basis of it`
    `defamation proceedings about it`
    `termination of my contract on the basis that it breached the contract`
    `liability for knowingly making a false or misleading statement`
    `an offence against section 137.1 or 137.2 or 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code`
    `liability for contravening a designated publication restriction`
    `liability for my own conduct that it reveals`

-- s 10(1) "If an individual makes a public interest disclosure: (a) the individual is not subject to any civil, criminal
-- or administrative liability (including disciplinary action) for making the public interest disclosure; and (b) no
-- contractual or other remedy may be enforced, and no contractual or other right may be exercised, against the individual
-- on the basis of the public interest disclosure." (2)(a) absolute privilege in defamation; (b) no termination of a
-- contract for breach. s 11(1), (2): "Section 10 does not apply" to knowingly false or misleading statements, or to the
-- four Criminal Code offences. s 11A: s 10 does not apply to contravening a designated publication restriction if the
-- discloser "(a) knows that the disclosure contravenes ... and (b) does not have a reasonable excuse". s 12: the
-- disclosure "does not affect his or her liability for the conduct".
GIVEN `a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN, l IS A `Liability faced`,
      `I knew it contravened the restriction` IS A BOOLEAN, `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 10-12 -- the discloser is protected` `a public interest disclosure` l `I knew it contravened the restriction` `I had a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF NOT `a public interest disclosure`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER l
         WHEN `liability for knowingly making a false or misleading statement` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `an offence against section 137.1 or 137.2 or 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `liability for contravening a designated publication restriction` THEN
             NOT (`I knew it contravened the restriction` AND (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`))
         WHEN `liability for my own conduct that it reveals` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `ss 12A, 12B -- immunity of the witness`

-- s 12A(1) applies to "an individual (the witness) who provides assistance in relation to a public interest disclosure
-- (other than the individual who makes the disclosure)". (2): assistance is giving information, a document or thing, or
-- answering a question, "that the person considers on reasonable grounds to be relevant to" an allocation decision, a
-- disclosure investigation (or proposed one), or an Ombudsman or IGIS review under s 55(3). (3)-(5) mirror s 10. s 12B(2),
-- (3) mirror s 11. s 12B(4): "Section 12A does not apply to proceedings against the witness for contravening a designated
-- publication restriction" -- with no knowledge or reasonable-excuse limb (finding 2). s 12B(5) mirrors s 12.
GIVEN `I made the disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN, `it is a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I gave information or a document or thing or answered a question` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds` IS A BOOLEAN,
      l IS A `Liability faced`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ss 12A, 12B -- the witness is protected` `I made the disclosure` `it is a public interest disclosure` `I gave information or a document or thing or answered a question` `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds` l MEANS
    IF `I made the disclosure`
       OR (NOT `it is a public interest disclosure`)
       OR (NOT `I gave information or a document or thing or answered a question`)
       OR (NOT `I considered it relevant on reasonable grounds`)
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER l
         WHEN `liability for knowingly making a false or misleading statement` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `an offence against section 137.1 or 137.2 or 144.1 or 145.1 of the Criminal Code` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `liability for contravening a designated publication restriction` THEN FALSE
         WHEN `liability for my own conduct that it reveals` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `s 13 -- taking a reprisal`

-- s 13(1): a person takes a reprisal against another if "(a) the first person engages in conduct that: (i) results in
-- detriment to the second person; or (ii) consists of, or results in, a threat to cause detriment to the second person;
-- and (b) when the conduct is engaged in, the first person believes or suspects that the second person, or any other
-- person: (i) has made ...; or (ii) may have made ...; or (iii) proposes to make ...; or (iv) could make a public
-- interest disclosure; and (c) the belief or suspicion is the reason, or part of the reason, for engaging in the
-- conduct." (2) lists detriment, "without limitation", ending "(j) any other damage to a person". (3): "a person does not
-- take a reprisal against another person to the extent that the person takes administrative action that is reasonable to
-- protect the other person from detriment." s 8 "takes a reprisal has the meaning given by section 13": closed.
GIVEN `detriment to me` IS A BOOLEAN, `a threat of detriment to me` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `they believed or suspected a disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN, `that was at least part of the reason` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reasonable administrative action to protect me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 13 -- a reprisal taken against me` `detriment to me` `a threat of detriment to me` `they believed or suspected a disclosure` `that was at least part of the reason` `reasonable administrative action to protect me` IF
        (`detriment to me` OR `a threat of detriment to me`)
    AND `they believed or suspected a disclosure`
    AND `that was at least part of the reason`
    AND (NOT `reasonable administrative action to protect me`)

§§ `ss 14-17, 22A -- orders for a reprisal`

DECLARE `Order for a reprisal` IS ONE OF
    `compensation from the person who took the reprisal`
    `compensation from their employer alone or jointly or in part`
    `an injunction restraining the reprisal or requiring them to do what they refused to do`
    `an apology`
    `any other order the court thinks appropriate`
    `reinstatement in my position or one at a comparable level`

-- s 22A(1): "A person is not entitled to make an application ... for an order under section 14, 15 or 16 ... in relation
-- to particular conduct if another application has been made" under Fair Work Act s 539 (for s 340 or 772) or s 394 for
-- the same conduct. (3): "This section does not apply if the other application ... has been discontinued or has failed
-- for want of jurisdiction."
GIVEN `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN, `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22A -- barred by a Fair Work application` `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction` IF
        `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct`
    AND (NOT `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction`)

-- s 14(1): if the Court "is satisfied ... that another person (the respondent) took or is taking a reprisal against the
-- applicant", it may order (a) in any case compensation by the respondent; (b) if "the respondent took or is taking the
-- reprisal in connection with the respondent's position as an employee", compensation by the respondent and the employer
-- in parts, jointly (and severally, (3)), or by the employer alone. (2): "must not make an order under paragraph (1)(b)
-- if the respondent's employer establishes that it took reasonable precautions, and exercised due diligence, to avoid the
-- reprisal." s 15(1): an injunction, an apology, "any other order the Court thinks appropriate". s 16: reinstatement if
-- "(b) the applicant is or was employed in a particular position with the respondent; and (c) the reprisal wholly or
-- partly consists, or consisted, of the respondent terminating, or purporting to terminate, the applicant's employment".
-- s 17: orders under ss 14, 15 and 16 may be made for the same conduct. The court's satisfaction is an input. The list is
-- what the court may order; each is the court's discretion ("may").
GIVEN `the court is satisfied of a reprisal` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `they acted in connection with their position as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `their employer took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I am or was employed by them` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the reprisal included terminating my employment` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Order for a reprisal`
`ss 14-16 -- the orders the court may make` `the court is satisfied of a reprisal` `they acted in connection with their position as an employee` `their employer took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence` `I am or was employed by them` `the reprisal included terminating my employment` `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction` MEANS
    IF     `s 22A -- barred by a Fair Work application` `I applied under the Fair Work Act for the same conduct` `that application was discontinued or failed for want of jurisdiction`
        OR (NOT `the court is satisfied of a reprisal`)
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE append `employer part` `the rest`
    WHERE
        `employer part` MEANS
            IF     `they acted in connection with their position as an employee`
               AND (NOT `their employer took reasonable precautions and exercised due diligence`)
            THEN LIST `compensation from the person who took the reprisal`, `compensation from their employer alone or jointly or in part`
            ELSE LIST `compensation from the person who took the reprisal`
        `the rest` MEANS
            IF `I am or was employed by them` AND `the reprisal included terminating my employment`
            THEN LIST `an injunction restraining the reprisal or requiring them to do what they refused to do`, `an apology`, `any other order the court thinks appropriate`, `reinstatement in my position or one at a comparable level`
            ELSE LIST `an injunction restraining the reprisal or requiring them to do what they refused to do`, `an apology`, `any other order the court thinks appropriate`

§§ `s 18 -- costs`

-- s 18(1): the applicant "must not be ordered by the court to pay costs incurred by another party to the proceedings,
-- except in accordance with subsection (2)." (2): "only if: (a) the court is satisfied that the applicant instituted the
-- proceedings vexatiously or without reasonable cause; or (b) the court is satisfied that the applicant's unreasonable act
-- or omission caused the other party to incur the costs." TRUE: a costs order may be made (the court's discretion).
GIVEN `vexatious or without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN, `my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18 -- I may be ordered to pay costs` `vexatious or without reasonable cause` `my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs` IF
        `vexatious or without reasonable cause`
    OR  `my unreasonable act or omission caused the costs`

§§ `ss 19, 20, 67 -- offences and penalties`

DECLARE `Offence` IS ONE OF
    `taking a reprisal by causing detriment (s 19(1))`
    `taking a reprisal by threatening detriment (s 19(2))`
    `disclosing identifying information about a discloser (s 20(1))`
    `using identifying information about a discloser (s 20(2))`
    `a legal practitioner disclosing or using what a legal practitioner disclosure told them (s 67(1))`

DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER

-- s 19(1), (2): "Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both." s 20(1), (2): "Penalty: Imprisonment for
-- 6 months or 30 penalty units, or both." s 67(1): "Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years or 120 penalty units, or both." The
-- value of a penalty unit is set by the Crimes Act 1914, not deposited.
GIVEN o IS AN `Offence`
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`the maximum penalty for` o MEANS
    CONSIDER o
    WHEN `disclosing identifying information about a discloser (s 20(1))` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 6, `penalty units` IS 30
    WHEN `using identifying information about a discloser (s 20(2))` THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 6, `penalty units` IS 30
    OTHERWISE `Maximum penalty` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 24, `penalty units` IS 120

§§ `s 20 -- my identity`

DECLARE `What they did with it` IS ONE OF
    `disclosed it to someone other than me`
    `disclosed it only to me`
    `used it`

-- s 20(3) (a)-(f), with (4) for what counts as "for the purposes of this Act".
DECLARE `Exception that applies` IS ONE OF
    `for the purposes of this Act such as assisting with the disclosure or giving legal advice about it or performing a function under the Act`
    `in performing the Ombudsman's function under section 5A of the Ombudsman Act 1976`
    `in performing the IGIS's function under section 8A of the IGIS Act 1986`
    `for the purposes of a Commonwealth law or a prescribed State or Territory law`
    `I consented or acted inconsistently with keeping my identity confidential`
    `the information had already been lawfully published`
    `no exception`

-- s 20(1): an offence if "(a) another person (the second person) has made a public interest disclosure; and (b) the first
-- person discloses information (identifying information) that: (i) was obtained by any person in that person's capacity
-- as a public official; and (ii) is likely to enable the identification of the second person as a person who has made a
-- public interest disclosure; and (c) the disclosure is to a person other than the second person." (2): "A person commits
-- an offence if the person uses identifying information." (3): "Subsections (1) and (2) do not apply if one or more of the
-- following applies" (a)-(f). TRUE: the elements of the offence are met (a court decides whether it was committed).
GIVEN `I made a public interest disclosure` IS A BOOLEAN, what IS A `What they did with it`,
      `obtained by someone as a public official` IS A BOOLEAN, `likely to identify me as the discloser` IS A BOOLEAN,
      e IS AN `Exception that applies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 20 -- an identifying information offence` `I made a public interest disclosure` what `obtained by someone as a public official` `likely to identify me as the discloser` e IF
        `I made a public interest disclosure`
    AND `obtained by someone as a public official`
    AND `likely to identify me as the discloser`
    AND (NOT (what EQUALS `disclosed it only to me`))
    AND e EQUALS `no exception`
